From: Amethyst Messenger maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Add XP-compatible desktop Windows fallbacks to TDLib

Keep the Vista path unchanged. For XP-targeted desktop builds, use critical
sections for shared mutex operations, legacy file and IPv4/IPv6 address APIs,
a GetTickCount wrap extender, and WSASendTo where TDLib sends no ancillary
message control data. Make the Windows API target configurable while retaining
TDLib's existing default.

Apply after tdlib-desktop-vista.patch.

diff --git a/CMake/TdSetUpCompiler.cmake b/CMake/TdSetUpCompiler.cmake
index ba54ed2..2a89ebb 100644
--- a/CMake/TdSetUpCompiler.cmake
+++ b/CMake/TdSetUpCompiler.cmake
@@ -96,7 +96,9 @@ function(td_set_up_compiler)
   endif()
 
   if (WIN32)
-    add_definitions(-DNTDDI_VERSION=0x06020000 -DWINVER=0x0602 -D_WIN32_WINNT=0x0602 -DPSAPI_VERSION=1 -DNOMINMAX -DUNICODE -D_UNICODE -DWIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN)
+    set(TD_WINDOWS_VERSION "0x0602" CACHE STRING "Minimum Windows API version")
+    set(TD_NTDDI_VERSION "0x06020000" CACHE STRING "Minimum Windows NTDDI version")
+    add_definitions(-DNTDDI_VERSION=${TD_NTDDI_VERSION} -DWINVER=${TD_WINDOWS_VERSION} -D_WIN32_WINNT=${TD_WINDOWS_VERSION} -DPSAPI_VERSION=1 -DNOMINMAX -DUNICODE -D_UNICODE -DWIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN)
   endif()
   if (CYGWIN)
     add_definitions(-D_DEFAULT_SOURCE=1 -DFD_SETSIZE=4096)
